I've no idea.

167
00:09:24,300 --> 00:09:25,600
（呼叫铃叮咚声）
(ALARM DINGS)

168
00:09:25,633 --> 00:09:27,067
-不好意思又打扰您了。
-没关系的。
-Sorry to bother you again.
-That's no problem.

169
00:09:27,100 --> 00:09:29,867
-请问这架飞机
值多少钱？
-五千万英镑。
-How much is this
aeroplane worth?
-£50 million.

170
00:09:29,900 --> 00:09:33,367
-五千万英镑啊。
-打个比方，可比法拉利贵多了。
-£50 million.
-That's more than a Ferrari,
for instance.

171
00:09:33,400 --> 00:09:34,967
-那可贵得不是一星半点。
-确实。
-That's quite a lot more.
-Yes.

172
00:09:35,000 --> 00:09:38,633
我腰一点不酸，
引擎很安静，
滤震也极佳。
I've no backache,
the engine's quiet,
the ride's good.

173
00:09:41,633 --> 00:09:43,567
真是辆优秀的GT跑车。
Good GT car.

174
00:09:43,600 --> 00:09:47,667
而且有意思的是，这趟我比上次
开DB9时还多撑过了一个加油站。
And I've got one filling
station further than I did
in the DB9, interestingly.

175
00:09:47,767 --> 00:09:49,867
不过话说回来，
它的油箱确实更大。
Mind you, it has got
a bigger tank.

176
00:09:49,900 --> 00:09:52,500
不知道
这飞机现在飞得多高。
I wonder
how high this is flying.

177
00:09:54,033 --> 00:09:55,767
（呼叫铃叮咚声）
(ALARM DINGS)

178
00:09:55,800 --> 00:09:59,800
要是没有云层遮挡，
咱们就能看到他在下面狂飙了。
If it weren't cloudy,
we'd be able to see them
screaming by.

179
00:10:02,800 --> 00:10:07,533
当飞机降落在日内瓦机场时，
我已经被远远甩在后头了，
When the aeroplane landed
at Geneva Airport,
I was way behind,

180
00:10:07,567 --> 00:10:09,867
还在第戎以北老远的地方。
still well north of Dijon.

181
00:10:09,900 --> 00:10:13,667
事实上我落后得实在太远，
琢磨着反正也没差了，
I was so far behind, in fact,
that I figured it wouldn't
make much difference

182
00:10:13,700 --> 00:10:18,633
不如靠边停下，
把我查出的异响根源给彻底修好。
if I pulled over and tried
to fix what I'd discovered
was the cause of the buzz.

183
00:10:19,533 --> 00:10:22,033
罪魁祸首就是雨刮器。
It was the wipers.

184
00:10:23,633 --> 00:10:28,433
行，来看看我用大力胶布
五花大绑的风挡雨刮器，
Right, let's see if my new
gaffer-taped-up
windscreen wipers

185
00:10:28,467 --> 00:10:30,767
到底能不能把这嗡嗡的杂音治住。
will stop the buzzing noise.

186
00:10:32,200 --> 00:10:33,500
见证奇迹的时刻。
Here we go.

187
00:10:33,967 --> 00:10:35,000
退出自动模式。
Out of auto.

188
00:10:49,833 --> 00:10:50,833
没戏。
No.

189
00:10:53,967 --> 00:10:56,233
克拉克森：
别告诉我
你们已经到日内瓦了。
CLARKSON:
Don't tell me
you're already in Geneva.

190
00:10:56,267 --> 00:11:00,067
我们确实已经在日内瓦了，
但截至目前，
滑雪板还没到。
We're already in Geneva,
but, so far,
our skis aren't.

191
00:11:00,100 --> 00:11:03,300
到了！
刚从小滑梯行李口吐出来。
Yes, they are.
They've just come out
of the little chute thing.

192
00:11:03,333 --> 00:11:05,267
抱歉，我得挂了。
Sorry, I'll have to go.

193
00:11:05,300 --> 00:11:07,200
今晚见啦。
See you tonight.

194
00:11:07,233 --> 00:11:09,000
克拉克森：
他们那边顺风顺水，
CLARKSON:
Things were going well
for them,

195
00:11:09,033 --> 00:11:11,667
我这边可就倒了大霉。
but they weren't going well
for me.

196
00:11:11,767 --> 00:11:16,533
现在我遇到大麻烦了，
因为我刚用胶带把雨刮器封死，
结果天下雨了！
Now I've got a big problem
'cause I've taped my wipers up
and it's raining!

197
00:11:16,567 --> 00:11:18,800
哎呀！（笑声）
Oh! (LAUGHS)

198
00:11:20,167 --> 00:11:21,600
我靠……
Oh, sh...

199
00:11:23,100 --> 00:11:27,467
-（嗡嗡异响）
-得，现在看明白了，
那绝对是个馊主意。
-(BUZZING)
-Yes, now, you see,
that was a bad plan.

200
00:11:27,500 --> 00:11:31,967
给大家个忠告：
如果你开的是法拉利612，
千万别拿胶带贴雨刮器。
Here's a tip.
If you've got a Ferrari 612,
don't tape your wipers up

201
00:11:32,000 --> 00:11:33,033
因为……
'cause...

202
00:11:34,667 --> 00:11:36,767
你早晚会把它们弄坏的。
you're going to break them.

203
00:11:36,800 --> 00:11:40,633
哈蒙德：与此同时，
我们只有五分钟时间
赶换乘的火车。
HAMMOND: Meanwhile,
we had only five minutes to
catch our train connection.

204
00:11:40,667 --> 00:11:42,133
而果不其然……
And as ever...

205
00:11:42,167 --> 00:11:43,767
梅：我们用不着跑。
MAY: We don't have to run.

206
00:11:43,800 --> 00:11:46,367
-不，你瞧，我们得跑。
-不，用不着，
还有五分钟呢。
-No, you see, we do.
-No, we don't.
It's five minutes away.

207
00:11:46,400 --> 00:11:49,200
跑就是比走快，
这是客观事实。
Running is faster
than walking.
It's just a fact.

208
00:11:49,233 --> 00:11:50,600
那倒未必。
Not really.

209
00:11:50,633 --> 00:11:53,167
要是我赶上了火车
而你错过了，那就自认倒霉吧。
If I get on the train
and you miss it, that's tough.

210
00:11:53,200 --> 00:11:58,267
我现在大概在
日内瓦以北250英里处，
I'm about
250 miles north of Geneva,

211
00:11:58,300 --> 00:12:02,667
所以眼下
他们领先了我整整250英里。
so they're 250 miles ahead
at this point.

212
00:12:02,767 --> 00:12:04,500
没错，我开始觉得
实际上……
Yes, I'm beginning to think
that actually...

213
00:12:06,300 --> 00:12:09,000
这局我可能真赢不了了。
I can't really win this.

214
00:12:09,033 --> 00:12:12,367
克拉克森：而詹姆斯
和理查德即将祭出那件
CLARKSON: And James
and Richard were about
to unleash the weapon

215
00:12:12,400 --> 00:12:14,833
最让汽车闻风丧胆的终极武器：
most feared by the car.

216
00:12:14,867 --> 00:12:20,400
瑞士公共交通！
它就从来、从不晚点。
Swiss public transport!
It is never ever late.

217
00:12:20,433 --> 00:12:22,800
接着，
更雪上加霜的是……
And then,
to make matters worse...

218
00:12:25,533 --> 00:12:30,100
克拉克森在电话里：
鼹鼠，跟你通报一声，
我碰上改道修路了。
CLARKSON ON THE PHONE:
Hamster, just so you know,
I'm in a contraflow.

219
00:12:30,133 --> 00:12:31,967
噢，太惨了吧。在哪呢？
Oh, that's poor. Where?

220
00:12:32,000 --> 00:12:34,000
法兰西岛。
哈蒙德：收到。
Ile de France.
HAMMOND: Okay.

221
00:12:34,033 --> 00:12:35,967
现在是两点，
两点零五分。
And it's now 2:00,
five past two.

222
00:12:36,000 --> 00:12:39,200
我大概还有两小时
能到瑞士。
I'm probably two hours
from Switzerland.

223
00:12:39,233 --> 00:12:41,600
哈蒙德：祝你输得开心，
回头再聊。
HAMMOND: Happy losing, and
we'll talk to you later on.

224
00:12:41,633 --> 00:12:43,633
他彻底完蛋了。
He's had it.

225
00:12:43,667 --> 00:12:46,000
克拉克森：
开阿斯顿·马丁赢火车轻轻松松。
CLARKSON:
Beating a train
in the Aston was easy.

226
00:12:46,033 --> 00:12:51,233
那是21世纪的工程杰作
对阵维多利亚时代的遗迹。
That's 21st-century
engineering
up against a Victorian relic.

227
00:12:51,267 --> 00:12:56,267
但想跑赢飞机，
现在看来
简直就是痴人说梦，
But to beat a plane,
that was beginning
to look like an impossibility,

228
00:12:56,300 --> 00:13:00,200
哪怕开的是
像法拉利612这么厉害的车。
even for a car
as good as the 612.

229
00:13:07,167 --> 00:13:09,833
说来有趣，今天早晨
我坐进这台车时，
It's funny, this morning
when I got into this car,

230
00:13:09,867 --> 00:13:12,933
人又困又累，看它的长相
也不太顺眼，
I was tired, I didn't like
the look of it very much,

231
00:13:12,967 --> 00:13:15,767
觉得它有点无聊，
接着车里还开始嘎吱异响，
thought it was a bit boring,
then the rattle started,

232
00:13:17,767 --> 00:13:21,233
但现在我开始体会到
并感受到那种法拉利的魔力了。
but I'm starting to see
and feel that Ferrari magic.

233
00:13:22,767 --> 00:13:26,533
那种无穷无尽的
动力储备，
That sense of
limitless power,

234
00:13:28,567 --> 00:13:30,533
狂暴的极速。
huge speed.

235
00:13:32,500 --> 00:13:34,933
上次他来这儿，
还在那吹呢：
“法国可太棒了，
Last time he was here,
he was going,
"France is so good,

236
00:13:34,967 --> 00:13:37,400
-交警恨不得你开得更快点。”
-嗯，没错。
-"The police, they just want
you to go faster."
-Um, yeah.

237
00:13:37,433 --> 00:13:40,600
（拿腔拿调的法国口音）
“先生，请继续开！
您可是大名鼎鼎的克拉克森先生！”
(IN FRENCH ACCENT)
"Monsieur, please carry on.
You are famous Mr Clarkson!"

238
00:13:40,633 --> 00:13:43,800
（警笛呼啸）
(SIREN WAILS)

239
00:13:43,833 --> 00:13:47,333
哈蒙德，
猜猜我在跟谁说话呢！
Hammond,
guess who I'm talking to!

240
00:13:47,367 --> 00:13:49,833
（大笑）
他在跟警察说话呢！
(LAUGHS)
He's talking to a policeman!

241
00:13:49,867 --> 00:13:56,433
克拉克森：我被罚了60英镑，
但更要命的是，
我耽误了整整25分钟。
CLARKSON: I was fined £60,
but more importantly,
I lost 25 minutes.

242
00:13:56,467 --> 00:14:02,033
这场比赛看起来
真的是
要输掉了。
The race really was
beginning to look
like it was lost.

243
00:14:02,067 --> 00:14:04,600
我掐指一算，杰里米现在
大概就在这附近，
Jeremy, I would calculate,
is somewhere around here,

244
00:14:04,633 --> 00:14:07,200
正靠在路边，
跟法国骑警打交道呢。
at the side of the road,
talking to a gendarme.

245
00:14:07,233 --> 00:14:10,533
再过几个小时，
他就会被关到上面这里，
一个叫巴士底狱的地方。
Within a few hours' time,
he'll be up here
at a place called Le Bastille.

246
00:14:10,567 --> 00:14:12,167
（两人大笑）
(BOTH LAUGHING)

247
00:14:19,500 --> 00:14:27,700
好吧。呃，这事儿咱们待会儿再看。
不过现在，该聊聊新闻了。
Okay. Um, we'll pick that up later on.
But for now, we must do The News.

248
00:14:27,733 --> 00:14:33,567
你当时开多快？
- 我就是不小心稍微超了点速而已。
How fast were you going?
- I strayed slightly over the speed limit.

249
00:14:33,600 --> 00:14:36,100
稍微？
然后就被逮了，不过人家执法
Strayed?
And I was caught, and they dealt with me

250
00:14:36,133 --> 00:14:42,167
既高效又客气，尽显
一个文明大国的风范，比如法国。
efficiently and corteously as befits
a civilised nation, like France is.

251
00:14:42,200 --> 00:14:47,800
得了吧。法国这破地方唯一的用处，
就是去意大利时路过一下，仅此而已。
No. France is a country you drive through
to get to Italy. That's all it's for.

252
00:14:47,833 --> 00:14:49,833
［现场观众大笑］
[AUDIENCE LAUGHING]

253
00:14:49,867 --> 00:14:52,400
法国人听了可不乐意。
- 听着，但事实摆在眼前，
They're not gonna like it.
- Look, the fact of the matter is

254
00:14:52,433 --> 00:14:56,600
人家的奶酪更好，红酒更好……
- 他们的奶酪才没我们的好！
they've got better cheese, better wine...
- They haven't got better cheese!

255
00:14:56,633 --> 00:15:00,867
他们就是一帮背信弃义、
天天烧地罢工的懒汉农民。
They are a bunch of treacherous,
land-burning, workshy peasants.

256
00:15:00,900 --> 00:15:03,900
［现场观众大笑并鼓掌］
[AUDIENCE LAUGHING AND APPLAUDING]

257
00:15:10,000 --> 00:15:14,500
你见过这座桥吗？就这座！
它坐落在哪个国家？英国还是法国？
Have you seen this? This bridge?
What country is it in? Britain or France?

258
00:15:14,533 --> 00:15:17,933
梅：在法国。
