而为了让这趟罪受得更刺激，
我们还要搞一场对决。
And to make things
even more arduous,
we're gonna have a race.

373
00:23:43,700 --> 00:23:46,867
梅：我们大老远跑来利勒哈默尔，是因为
就在这条雪车道旁边，
MAY: Now, we've come
to Lillehammer, because
alongside the bobsleigh run,

374
00:23:46,900 --> 00:23:48,367
正好有这么一条公路。
we have this road.

375
00:23:48,400 --> 00:23:50,000
它们从同一个起点出发，
They start in the same place,

376
00:23:50,033 --> 00:23:53,233
顺着山势一路向下，
最后在同一个终点汇合。
they run down the hill,
and they finish
in the same place.

377
00:23:53,267 --> 00:23:56,600
这条路的长度
几乎和雪车道完全一致。
The road is almost exactly
the same length
as the bob run.

378
00:23:56,633 --> 00:24:01,633
而且和雪道一样，
路面湿滑、凶险，满是要命的急弯。
And like the bob run,
it's slippery, dangerous
and full of difficult corners.

379
00:24:03,267 --> 00:24:05,367
这就需要一辆非比寻常的座驾。
It requires a special vehicle.

380
00:24:10,333 --> 00:24:11,933
于是我们把它给请来了。
So that's what we've got.

381
00:24:11,967 --> 00:24:14,500
这是一辆三菱Evo
WRC世界拉力赛车，
It's a Mitsubishi Evo
World Rally Car

382
00:24:14,533 --> 00:24:18,433
坐拥300匹马力、
涡轮增压发动机、四轮驱动，
with a 300 horsepower,
turbo-charged engine,
four-wheel drive,

383
00:24:18,467 --> 00:24:20,967
以及带防滑钉的雪地胎。
and studded tyres.

384
00:24:21,000 --> 00:24:24,300
所以挑战来了：
拉力赛车究竟能不能跑赢雪车？
So that's the challenge.
Can the rally car
beat the bobsleigh?

385
00:24:24,333 --> 00:24:30,167
我个人坚信能赢，
虽说哈蒙德一口咬定绝对没戏。
I happen to think it can,
although Hammond tells me
it definitely can't.

386
00:24:30,200 --> 00:24:33,333
瞧，这是我的雪车道，
从这儿出发，一路扭啊扭扭到下面，
Now, this is my bobsleigh run,
it starts here and wiggles
all the way down here

387
00:24:33,367 --> 00:24:34,633
终点就在那儿。
and finishes there.

388
00:24:34,667 --> 00:24:36,867
而这条绿色的则是公路，
And this is the road,
which is in green,

389
00:24:36,867 --> 00:24:38,700
同样从这儿出发，一路扭啊扭
绕过那头去，
and it starts here
and wiggles
all the way up there,

390
00:24:38,733 --> 00:24:40,600
但冲线的地方完全一样。
but finishes in
exactly the same place.

391
00:24:40,633 --> 00:24:41,733
哈蒙德：
没错，但关键问题在这儿。
HAMMOND:
Yes, but here's the point.

392
00:24:41,767 --> 00:24:43,400
我的雪车从那儿出发，
My bobsleigh
can get from there,

393
00:24:43,433 --> 00:24:45,933
一路飚到最底下，
用时不到一分钟。
all the way down to there,
in less than a minute.

394
00:24:45,967 --> 00:24:47,767
你死定了。
You've had it.

395
00:24:47,867 --> 00:24:50,467
可你想想，能把你从那儿
带到这儿的，只有重力而已。
But, you see, all you've got
to take you from
there to there is gravity.

396
00:24:50,500 --> 00:24:52,600
-对啊。
-重力算个屁。
-Yes.
-That's nothing.

397
00:24:52,633 --> 00:24:57,433
可我有300匹马力、
硕大无比的涡轮增压器，每条胎上还嵌着420颗钢钉，
Well, I've got 300 horsepower
and a huge, huge turbocharger,
and 420 spikes in each tyre

398
00:24:57,467 --> 00:24:59,967
-外加重力，一路狂飙下去。
-是，但……
-and gravity
to get down there.
-Yes, but...

399
00:25:00,000 --> 00:25:02,667
可我的雪车那是专为
冰面滑行量身定做的。
But my bobsleigh
was custom-built
for going on ice.

400
00:25:02,700 --> 00:25:05,733
你的车无非是靠着
花哨的钉胎和改装件硬凑出来的。
Your car has had to be
sort of adapted
with clever tyres and stuff.

401
00:25:05,767 --> 00:25:07,333
-你穿的是紧身裤。
-对啊。
-You're wearing tights.
-I am.

402
00:25:07,367 --> 00:25:09,867
我可没法听一个穿紧身裤的男人
跟我讲物理。
I can't take lectures
on physics
from the man in tights.

403
00:25:09,900 --> 00:25:11,533
-我知道我穿着紧身裤。
-聊跳芭蕾还行。
-I am aware of the tights.
-Dancing, yes.

404
00:25:11,567 --> 00:25:12,867
-讲物理，算了吧。（笑）
-（笑）
-Physics, no. (LAUGHS)
-(LAUGHS)

405
00:25:15,033 --> 00:25:18,267
梅：不过说实话，
雪橇确实是个
很难击败的对手，
MAY: The truth is, though,
the bob is going
to be hard to beat,

406
00:25:18,300 --> 00:25:21,000
这也基本上排除了
让我来开车的可能。
which kind of counts me out
for driving the car.

407
00:25:24,400 --> 00:25:26,700
所以我们找来了
亨宁·索尔伯格，
So instead,
we've got Henning Solberg,

408
00:25:26,733 --> 00:25:29,400
挪威全国拉力锦标赛冠军。
the Norwegian
National Rally Champion.

409
00:25:30,700 --> 00:25:32,900
一、二、三。
One, two, three.

410
00:25:32,933 --> 00:25:36,267
哈蒙德：有舵雪橇能不能赢，
全看起跑有多猛。
HAMMOND: The bobsleigh's
chance of victory all depends
on how good our start is.

411
00:25:36,300 --> 00:25:41,000
这意味着我和挪威奥运雪橇队
必须进行高强度的集训。
That means intense preparation
for me and the Norwegian
Olympic bobsleigh team.

412
00:25:43,567 --> 00:25:48,867
在我们苦练推车助跑的同时，
舵手正在脑海中默演整条赛道。
And while we practise running,
the driver visualises
the course in his head.

413
00:25:52,900 --> 00:25:56,767
这一切
让骨子里懒透了的梅
看足了乐子。
All this
provided much merriment
for the bone idle May.

414
00:25:56,867 --> 00:25:58,667
-你在热身吗？
-对啊。
-Are you warming up?
-Yes.

415
00:25:58,700 --> 00:26:01,500
我也在热身呢。
I'm warming up as well.

416
00:26:01,533 --> 00:26:04,067
哈蒙德：说实话，
我可一点儿都笑不出来，
HAMMOND: To be honest,
I couldn't
see the funny side of it

417
00:26:04,100 --> 00:26:09,067
因为我真的很怕
拖了全队的后腿。
because I was really worried
about letting the team down.

418
00:26:09,100 --> 00:26:13,233
起跑耽误的任何一点时间，
在上面慢一秒，到了终点就会放大成三倍。
Any time you lose here,
a second is multiplied
by three at the bottom.

419
00:26:13,267 --> 00:26:15,133
也就是说，
差了整整三秒。
So, that would be
three seconds.

420
00:26:15,167 --> 00:26:18,600
而且我也很担心
自己的小身板到底顶不顶得住。
And I was also worried about
whether my body would cope.

421
00:26:18,633 --> 00:26:20,700
关键在于，
进弯的时候，
Key thing is,
as you go into the corners,

422
00:26:20,733 --> 00:26:23,200
一定要憋住气，
拼命深吸一口气憋住，
to hold your breath,
to get as much breath in
as you can

423
00:26:23,233 --> 00:26:25,333
因为这样才能稳住你的身体。
'cause that actually
holds your body up.

424
00:26:25,367 --> 00:26:28,000
在弯道承受重力加速度时，
它能实打实地撑住你的骨架。
It literally supports you
when you're being subjected
to G-forces in the corners.

425
00:26:28,033 --> 00:26:32,667
据说底下有那么几个地方，
G值甚至能飙到6.5G。
Apparently in a couple
of places down there,
it hits six-and-a-half G.

426
00:26:32,700 --> 00:26:34,633
舵手告诉我，
他玩这个玩了六年，
Driver told me
he's been doing this six years

427
00:26:34,667 --> 00:26:37,100
身高缩水了整整三厘米。
and he's three centimetres
shorter.

428
00:26:38,100 --> 00:26:40,267
我可再矮不起三厘米了。
I can't afford to lose
three centimetres.

429
00:26:44,900 --> 00:26:48,600
哈蒙德：詹姆斯系好了安全带，
我也准备好起跑了。
HAMMOND: James was strapped in
and I was ready to run.

430
00:26:50,467 --> 00:26:53,500
我们的拉力车手几乎一句英语都不会说。
Our race rally driver could
hardly speak any English.

431
00:26:53,533 --> 00:26:57,867
但这并不妨碍詹姆斯用那种居高临下的
英式腔调给他做赛前动员。
But that didn't stop James
giving him a patronising
British pep talk.

432
00:26:57,867 --> 00:27:02,167
听好了，亨宁，
内燃机的尊严，
Righto, Henning,
it's the reputation
of internal combustion

433
00:27:02,200 --> 00:27:06,867
在接下来的一分多钟里可全压在你肩上了。
resting on your shoulders
over the next minute or so.

434
00:27:09,133 --> 00:27:12,033
我打算用我信赖的秒表给赛车计时。
I was going to time the car
with my trusty stopwatch.

435
00:27:12,067 --> 00:27:15,733
哈蒙德的雪橇则由赛道官方人员计时。
And Hammond's bob would be
timed by the course officials.

436
00:27:15,767 --> 00:27:18,133
动真格的了。
This was it.

437
00:27:20,367 --> 00:27:21,367
所有人：走！
ALL: Go.

438
00:27:23,167 --> 00:27:24,200
（蜂鸣声）
(BUZZING)

439
00:27:35,700 --> 00:27:37,933
那是树啊……你个疯子！
The trees...you nutter!

440
00:27:38,867 --> 00:27:40,433
哈蒙德：
我们开始入弯了。
HAMMOND:
We're starting to turn.

441
00:27:40,467 --> 00:27:44,967
噢！好急的弯。
又过一个弯，总共16个弯道。
Oh! That's a turn.
That's a turn. 16 corners.

442
00:27:45,000 --> 00:27:47,167
才刚过去三个。
That's three of them done.

443
00:27:50,467 --> 00:27:53,733
梅：两公里冰道，
要在一分钟内跑完。
MAY: Two kilometres,
on ice, in a minute.

444
00:27:53,767 --> 00:27:56,667
天哪，亨宁
这下可有得拼了！
Boy, has Henning
got it all to do!

445
00:27:56,700 --> 00:27:58,367
噢！疼死我了！
撞到我的头了！
Oh! That hurts a lot!
That's my head!

446
00:28:00,067 --> 00:28:01,267
（哔——）
(BLEEP)

447
00:28:02,700 --> 00:28:04,333
哈蒙德：
雪车起步可能有点慢，
HAMMOND:
The bob may have started slow,

448
00:28:04,367 --> 00:28:07,567
但后面只会越来越快，
越来越快，
but it was just getting faster
and faster,

449
00:28:07,600 --> 00:28:09,767
而且这帮家伙
根本不踩刹车。
and these guys
never use the brakes.

450
00:28:10,567 --> 00:28:11,867
不！别，别，别！
No! No, no, no!

451
00:28:13,133 --> 00:28:14,867
哈蒙德：
前面是一组
连续复合弯……
HAMMOND:
There's a complex
coming up...

452
00:28:14,867 --> 00:28:18,467
噢，过了一个！
又来一个。
Oh, that's one!
And there's another.

453
00:28:18,500 --> 00:28:22,767
梅：赛程过半，
跑完1000米时，
胜负依然悬而未决。
MAY: At mid-point,
1,000 metres in,
it was anybody's guess.

454
00:28:24,767 --> 00:28:26,300
刹车，踩刹车啊，哥们儿！
Brake, use the brakes, man!

455
00:28:30,400 --> 00:28:34,100
哈蒙德：
噢，往这儿塞只袜子垫垫！
我脑袋一直在撞。
HAMMOND:
Oh, put a sock in here!
I'm banging my head.

456
00:28:35,333 --> 00:28:36,633
噢！
Oh!

457
00:28:50,233 --> 00:28:53,600
噢，我的头！深呼吸。
Oh, my head! Big breaths.

458
00:28:53,633 --> 00:28:58,867
梅：
亨宁简直太神了！
在冰面上怎么可能开这么快。
MAY:
Henning was just awesome!
You can't go this fast on ice.

459
00:28:58,900 --> 00:29:01,133
（哔——）
(BLEEP)

460
00:29:01,167 --> 00:29:03,667
哈蒙德：他蹭到护墙了。
他会害死我们的。
HAMMOND: He hit the side.
He's going to kill us.

461
00:29:05,467 --> 00:29:06,933
（尖叫）
(SCREAMING)

462
00:29:07,900 --> 00:29:09,833
我可不想穿着紧身衣去死！
I don't want to die in tights!

463
00:29:26,467 --> 00:29:27,767
59秒68。
59.68.

464
00:29:29,033 --> 00:29:30,367
我们赢了吗？
Did we win?

465
00:29:30,400 --> 00:29:31,600
他跑了多少？
What did he do?

466
00:29:33,000 --> 00:29:34,100
我的天！
Strewth!

467
00:29:34,567 --> 00:29:35,633
（倒吸冷气）
(GASPS)

468
00:29:35,667 --> 00:29:37,567
（苦笑）我整个人都散架了。
(SCOFFS) I'm broken.

469
00:29:37,600 --> 00:29:40,367
-你们成绩是多少？
-59秒68。
-What have you done it in?
-59.68.

470
00:29:40,400 --> 00:29:42,600
念啊……快点，快念！
Go on... Come on, come on!

471
00:29:43,600 --> 00:29:46,000
1分02秒24。
One minute, two seconds, 24.

472
00:29:46,033 --> 00:29:47,367
太棒了！我们赢了！
Yes! We've won!

473
00:29:48,600 --> 00:29:51,100
哥几个！太给力了！
Guys! The boys!

474
00:29:51,133 --> 00:29:53,433
-太爽了。
-希望我没给你们
拖太多后腿。
-That was good.
-Hope I didn't slow
you up too much.

475
00:29:53,467 --> 00:29:57,700
简直不可思议！我们做到了。
这趟真是太绝了。
That was fantastic! We did it.
That really was something.

476
00:29:57,733 --> 00:29:59,600
（大笑）
太牛了！赢喽！
(LAUGHING)
Awesome! Yes!

477
00:30:03,233 --> 00:30:05,067
（观众鼓掌欢呼）
(AUDIENCE APPLAUDING)

478
00:30:11,567 --> 00:30:13,233
我不得不说……
I have to say...

479
00:30:14,700 --> 00:30:17,400
我不得不说，詹姆斯，
你当时看起来魂都吓飞了！
I have to say, James,
you looked petrified!

480
00:30:17,433 --> 00:30:18,500
-废话，我是真吓傻了。
-（全场大笑）
-Well, I was.
-(ALL LAUGHING)

481
00:30:18,533 --> 00:30:20,367
你确实……
不过平心而论……
You did...
I will say, though...

482
00:30:20,400 --> 00:30:22,733
这些年我玩过的所有作死玩意儿里，
什么战斗机之类的，
Of all the things
I've ever done over the years,
jet fighters and so on,

483
00:30:22,767 --> 00:30:25,333
坐有舵雪橇
绝对是最吓人的。
bobsleighing
is easily the scariest.

484
00:30:25,367 --> 00:30:27,467
-千真万确。
-是啊，吓得要死。
而且还巨疼。
-It really is.
-Yeah, it's very frightening.
It's painful, too.

485
00:30:27,500 --> 00:30:30,967
因为你必须穿这种带钉子的怪异运动鞋，
才能在冰面上抓地。
Because you have to wear these
funny trainers with spikes on
so you can get grip the ice.

486
00:30:31,000 --> 00:30:32,767
但坑爹的是，
当后座那哥们儿跳进来的时候，
But the thing is,
when the guy leaps in
behind you,

487
00:30:32,867 --> 00:30:35,500
我发现，
那钉子直接扎进我腿里了。
they also stick in your leg,
I noticed.

488
00:30:35,533 --> 00:30:39,333
说真的，全靠我的骨头
才没让他直接把我捅个对穿。痛死了。
In fact, it was only my bones
that stopped him going all
the way through me. It hurts.

489
00:30:39,367 --> 00:30:41,933
还有一件事，
我当时在因斯布鲁克坐进去准备滑时，
Plus, there's another thing,
when I got in it
to do my run in Innsbruck,

490
00:30:41,967 --> 00:30:45,133
他们跟我说，就算雪橇翻了，
它也一样会一路滑到底，
they said it will continue
to go to the bottom,
even if it turns over,

491
00:30:45,167 --> 00:30:48,333
只不过是拿里面最高那人的脑袋磨着地滑。
it'll just be on the head
of the tallest person in it.

492
00:30:48,367 --> 00:30:50,067
（全场大笑）
(ALL LAUGHING)

493
00:30:50,100 --> 00:30:51,533
那你在里面肯定安全了。
You would have been
okay on that.

494
00:30:51,567 --> 00:30:53,867
-你直接算人形防滚架。
-没错。行了，
-You're a kind of
human rollbar.
-Yeah. Anyway,

495
00:30:53,867 --> 00:30:56,400
咱们得继续了，
该见见今天的嘉宾了。
we got to move on,
we've got to meet our guest.

496
00:30:56,433 --> 00:30:58,467
他是个纯爷们儿，
除非他不想当。
He's a man,
except when he isn't.

497
00:30:58,500 --> 00:31:01,167
女士们，先生们，
掌声欢迎埃迪·伊扎德！
Ladies and gentlemen,
please welcome Eddie Izzard!

498
00:31:01,200 --> 00:31:03,100
（观众欢呼）
(AUDIENCE CHEERING)

499
00:31:05,500 --> 00:31:08,333
-最近如何？
-挺好。呃，勉强活着吧。
-How are you?
-Fine. Well, just about.

500
00:31:12,867 --> 00:31:17,300
-听说你考了飞行执照？
-我有飞行执照。
-Now, you've got
a pilot's licence.
-I have a pilot's licence.

501
00:31:17,333 --> 00:31:21,533
所以我就很好奇，
你真能开“喷火”战斗机吗？
And so, I was just wondering,
can you actually
fly a Spitfire?

502
00:31:21,567 --> 00:31:25,700
我觉得行。真的，
如果现在让我坐进去，假设在《大逃亡》里，
I think, yeah,
I think if I got it now,
if I was in The Great Escape

503
00:31:25,733 --> 00:31:28,467
我是詹姆斯·加纳，
and I was James Garner,

504
00:31:28,500 --> 00:31:30,267
眼前正停着一架“喷火”，
and there was
a Spitfire there,

505
00:31:30,300 --> 00:31:32,400
（结巴）
唐纳德·普莱森斯在旁边问：
“这些飞机你开得了吗？”
