这本该是一场毫无悬念的碾压局。
The figures suggest
this will be a walkover.

757
00:43:46,400 --> 00:43:50,567
奥迪多了整整20匹马力，
而且还轻了足足三分之一吨。
The Audi has 20 more
horsepower and is a third
of a tonne lighter.

758
00:43:50,600 --> 00:43:54,233
说实话，
1983年离现在也没过去多久嘛。
And to be honest,
1983 isn't that long ago.

759
00:43:54,267 --> 00:43:57,100
虽说我也知道EVO就是个
装了四个轮子的奔腾处理器，
Now, I know the Evo's
a Pentium processor
with wheels,

760
00:43:57,133 --> 00:43:59,867
但也很难想象
它到底要怎么翻盘赢这一场。
but it's hard to see
how it can win this.

761
00:43:59,900 --> 00:44:04,233
不过话说回来，我不得不承认，
过了“锤头弯”之后，
它居然一点点超前了。
Although, that said, I have to
say, through the Hammerhead,
it is actually edging ahead.

762
00:44:04,267 --> 00:44:07,867
奥迪显然吃了大亏，
因为它的发动机悬在前轴前面，
The Audi is obviously
suffering 'cause its engine is
slung ahead of the front axle,

763
00:44:07,900 --> 00:44:09,767
这会导致
极其严重的推头，
which causes
massive under-steer,

764
00:44:09,867 --> 00:44:12,867
又或者，
是那一堆车灯的重量
把它给拖累了。
or perhaps it's the weight
of all those lights
slowing it down.

765
00:44:12,867 --> 00:44:17,067
但不管是什么原因，
现在带着原厂地毯、享有质保的这台Evo，
Whatever the reason,
it's the Evo with the carpets
and the warranty

766
00:44:17,100 --> 00:44:19,733
竟然要赢下这场比赛了！
我简直不敢相信！
that's going to win this!
I cannot believe it!

767
00:44:19,767 --> 00:44:21,700
当它们杀进最后一个弯道……
As they come into
the last corner...

768
00:44:21,733 --> 00:44:23,600
它居然真的赢了！
It's actually won!

769
00:44:23,633 --> 00:44:24,967
（掌声）
(APPLAUSE)

770
00:44:28,000 --> 00:44:29,333
我都惊呆了。
I'm stunned.

771
00:44:32,033 --> 00:44:35,233
Evo以1.5秒的优势赢了这一局，
The Evo won that
by 1.5 seconds,

772
00:44:35,267 --> 00:44:38,700
这意味着市售展厅车拿下了两分，
而纯种赛车才拿了一分。
which means it's two
to the showroom cars
and only one to the racers.

773
00:44:38,733 --> 00:44:40,500
我觉得这简直太不可思议了。
I think that's remarkable.

774
00:44:40,533 --> 00:44:43,633
确实令人叹为观止，仔细想想，
就在不久以前，
It is astonishing because
if you think about it,
not that long ago,

775
00:44:43,667 --> 00:44:49,900
成千上万的人还要奔波几百英里，
在威尔士的树林里整宿整宿地干站着，
people were travelling
hundreds of miles to stand up
in a wood, all night, in Wales

776
00:44:49,933 --> 00:44:53,067
就为了看一眼这种赛车全油门呼啸而过。
just to watch one of these
go by at full chat.

777
00:44:53,100 --> 00:44:57,867
而现在，你随便买一辆普通公路车，
就能跑得和它一样快。
And now, you can buy
a road car
which is just as fast.

778
00:44:57,867 --> 00:44:59,533
行了，言归正传。
Right. It's time to move on.

779
00:44:59,567 --> 00:45:02,100
如果你刚刚打开电视，
我们正在进行一场终极对决。
Now, if you've just joined us,
this is really
the ultimate race.

780
00:45:02,133 --> 00:45:05,500
因为杰里米正开着一辆法拉利——
就是这种款式的，
Because Jeremy is trying to
drive one of these Ferraris,
one like this,

781
00:45:05,533 --> 00:45:07,367
从我们位于吉尔福德的演播室出发，
from our studio here
in Guildford

782
00:45:07,400 --> 00:45:11,367
一路狂奔到瑞士韦尔比耶的
洛奇酒店。
all the way down to
the Lodge Hotel in Verbier,
which is in Switzerland.

783
00:45:11,400 --> 00:45:16,200
而他的目标，是要比我和詹姆斯坐飞机
还要更快抵达那里。
And he's trying to do that
faster than James and I
can get there on a plane.

784
00:45:16,233 --> 00:45:19,033
刚刚在上一段里，我和詹姆斯大概在这块儿，
Now, when we left the action,
James and I were about here
somewhere,

785
00:45:19,067 --> 00:45:20,867
而杰里米差不多在这一带，
and Jeremy was around here,

786
00:45:20,867 --> 00:45:26,000
落后我们大约250英里，
而且他刚刚还因为超速被交警拦了。
about 250 miles behind us,
and he'd just been stopped
for speeding.

787
00:45:26,033 --> 00:45:28,100
当时我们感觉胜券在握。
We were feeling
pretty confident.

788
00:45:30,967 --> 00:45:33,000
克拉克森：时间来到一个小时之后，
CLARKSON: We pick up the story
an hour later,

789
00:45:33,033 --> 00:45:35,767
詹姆斯和理查德正坐在阿尔卑斯山区的火车上，
with James and Richard
on a train in the Alps,

790
00:45:35,867 --> 00:45:40,200
而我已经下了高速，
跑进了洛桑湖北部的山区。
and me off the motorway,
in the hills
north of Lake Lausanne.

791
00:45:42,200 --> 00:45:45,700
现在拼的不再是马力，
而是开始考验操控性了，
So, now it stops being
about power and starts being
about handling,

792
00:45:45,733 --> 00:45:47,367
在这方面，它可是把好手。
and on that front
it's very good.

793
00:45:47,400 --> 00:45:50,333
因为发动机虽在前部，但位于前轮轴心之后，
Because the engine may be
in the front but it's
behind the front wheels,

794
00:45:50,367 --> 00:45:52,067
所以它实际上属于前中置布局。
so it's actually mid-engined.

795
00:45:52,100 --> 00:45:55,667
变速箱又位于后轴，
带来了完美的重量分配。
And the gearbox
is at the back for perfect
weight distribution.

796
00:45:56,667 --> 00:45:59,133
这下可有得爽了。
This should be a riot.

797
00:46:00,700 --> 00:46:02,333
-你在哪儿？
-他正在追上来。
-Where are you?
-He's catching up.

798
00:46:03,600 --> 00:46:05,867
我们正往……
We're on our way towards...

799
00:46:06,367 --> 00:46:07,600
马蒂尼方向走。
Martigny.

800
00:46:07,633 --> 00:46:10,000
哈蒙德：
天哪，你还真要追上来了！
HAMMOND:
God, you are catching up!

801
00:46:10,033 --> 00:46:14,600
畅通的道路帮了杰里米大忙，
而我们现在又没了喷气发动机的推力优势。
Lay roads had been kind to
Jeremy, and now we no longer
had jet engine power.

802
00:46:14,633 --> 00:46:16,933
他开始逐渐缩小差距了。
He was starting to
close the gap.

803
00:46:18,200 --> 00:46:19,700
克拉克森：我看到雪了。
CLARKSON: I've got snow.

804
00:46:22,933 --> 00:46:25,433
地上有积雪了，
There is snow on the ground,

805
00:46:25,467 --> 00:46:27,933
我现在已经不止是喜欢这辆车了。
and I don't just love this car
any more.

806
00:46:27,967 --> 00:46:30,667
真希望你们也能看看我现在在哪。
I wish you could be
where I am now.

807
00:46:32,767 --> 00:46:36,700
梅：那也比我们强，
我们正被困在马蒂尼车站的站台上，
MAY: Which is better than
where we were, on the platform
at Martigny station

808
00:46:36,733 --> 00:46:40,967
得干等一个小时，
之后还得倒另一趟火车再转大巴。
with an hour's wait,
and then another train
and a bus to catch.

809
00:46:41,000 --> 00:46:43,967
等那个“圣伯纳德快线”
整整等了一个小时！
An hour with the
Saint Bernard Express!

810
00:46:44,000 --> 00:46:45,200
（两人大笑）
(BOTH LAUGHING)

811
00:46:45,233 --> 00:46:47,867
哈蒙德：快瞧那个！
梅：狗狗专列！
HAMMOND: Look at that!
MAY: The dog train!

812
00:46:47,867 --> 00:46:52,100
哈蒙德：那一个小时简直要命，
因为就在我们等车的时候，
HAMMOND: That hour was really
killing us, because while
we were waiting for the train,

813
00:46:52,133 --> 00:46:54,633
杰里米正在一路狂飙赶里程。
Jeremy was racking up
the miles.

814
00:46:56,767 --> 00:47:00,433
-你在哪儿呢？
-洛桑湖北边。
-Where are you?
-North of Lake Lausanne.

815
00:47:00,467 --> 00:47:02,433
你们现在到马蒂尼了，是吧？
You're now in Martigny,
are you?

816
00:47:02,467 --> 00:47:04,167
对，但我们得在这儿死等一个小时。
Yes, but we're going
to be here for an hour.

817
00:47:04,200 --> 00:47:07,200
可你们离韦尔比耶近得吐口唾沫都能溅到了！
Yeah, but you can spit
and you can hit Verbier!

818
00:47:07,233 --> 00:47:09,300
我知道。
但我们接下来要坐的那趟车……
I know.
But the next train
that we've got

819
00:47:09,333 --> 00:47:12,867
是……（嘟囔）……
奥德利牧师童话里那种小火车。
is (MUMBLES)... The
Reverend W Awdry's stories.

820
00:47:12,867 --> 00:47:15,100
-（杰里米大笑）
-之后我们还得再倒一趟大巴。
-(JEREMY LAUGHING)
-And then we've got
a bus as well.

821
00:47:15,133 --> 00:47:17,767
过去这一个小时你真追上来不少。
You've really caught up in
the last hour.

822
00:47:17,867 --> 00:47:19,667
你把距离缩短了一半都不止。
You've more than halved
the distance.

823
00:47:21,100 --> 00:47:24,200
克拉克森：
终于到瑞士边境了！
CLARKSON:
At last, the Swiss border!

824
00:47:24,233 --> 00:47:26,867
这么一来我就要离开欧盟了，
So, now I shall be leaving
the EU

825
00:47:26,867 --> 00:47:31,767
而且不管怎么说，从汽车的角度来看，
我这是要迈入“黑暗时代”了。
and automotively speaking,
at any rate,
entering the Dark Ages.

826
00:47:33,067 --> 00:47:36,367
瑞士这地方的毛病就在于，
他们对……
The trouble with Switzerland
is that they have

827
00:47:36,400 --> 00:47:39,267
超速零容忍，
no tolerance at all of speed

828
00:47:39,867 --> 00:47:42,633
对汽车和污染也是深恶痛绝。
and cars and pollution.

829
00:47:43,900 --> 00:47:46,933
当年史蒂夫·麦奎因要是真像在电影
《大逃亡》里那样，
If Steve McQueen had
actually made that jump

830
00:47:46,967 --> 00:47:49,700
骑着摩托车飞跃边境跳进瑞士，
on his bike
in The Great Escape,
into Switzerland,

831
00:47:49,733 --> 00:47:52,167
他们当场就会以危险驾驶罪把他给抓起来。
they'd have arrested him
for reckless driving.

832
00:47:54,733 --> 00:47:57,533
这将是最后一次进站加油。
This was going to be
the final fill-up.

833
00:47:57,567 --> 00:48:00,867
以这台法拉利每加仑跑15英里的油耗，
With the Ferrari averaging
15 miles to the gallon,

834
00:48:00,867 --> 00:48:05,600
接下来就是油门到底、直捣韦尔比耶的冲刺了。
it would now be a non-stop
thrash to Verbier.

835
00:48:05,633 --> 00:48:09,100
与此同时理查德和詹姆斯正登上
圣伯纳德快线，
Meanwhile Richard and James
were boarding
the Saint Bernard Express

836
00:48:09,133 --> 00:48:13,367
开始他们的最后一程火车，
但我已经在发了疯似地狂追了。
for their last train journey,
but I was seriously
catching them up.

837
00:48:15,200 --> 00:48:17,600
好吧，现在真是紧张到窒息了，因为……
Well, this is just
super-tense now, because

838
00:48:17,633 --> 00:48:21,967
我们还得在这趟火车上坐十分钟左右，
去地图上的这个地方，勒沙布勒。
we've got another 10 minutes
or so on this train to get to,
it's on this map, Le Chable.

839
00:48:23,200 --> 00:48:25,900
然后从那里过去还要多久，坐……
And then from there,
how long, it's a...

840
00:48:25,933 --> 00:48:27,167
坐大巴十五分钟。
Fifteen minutes on the bus.

841
00:48:28,500 --> 00:48:30,767
然后还得走上
十分钟。
And then it's
a 10-minute walk.

842
00:48:30,800 --> 00:48:33,567
-你清楚咱们最后还得走过去吧？
-知道。
-You do know we've got
that walk at the end?
-Yeah.

843
00:48:33,600 --> 00:48:35,267
走过去。
Walk.

844
00:48:35,300 --> 00:48:38,967
-要是你……
-除非我看见他了，
那我绝对会在电视直播里跑起来。
-Now if you...
-Unless I see him,
then I will run on television.

845
00:48:40,367 --> 00:48:43,167
克拉克森：
他们现在只领先我
60英里了。
CLARKSON:
They're only 60 miles
ahead of me now.

846
00:48:44,433 --> 00:48:46,200
就只差60英里了。
Only 60 miles ahead.

847
00:48:47,667 --> 00:48:50,133
我已经追回了140英里。
I've made up 140 miles.

848
00:48:51,733 --> 00:48:53,700
而且我还没完呢。
And I haven't finished yet.

849
00:48:55,400 --> 00:49:01,267
杰里米的位置，大概就在
紧跟我们屁股后头
和咱们目的地之间的某个地方。
Jeremy is somewhere between
probably just behind us
and where we're going.

850
00:49:01,300 --> 00:49:03,233
我是说，真的就咬得这么紧。
I mean, it's that close.

851
00:49:03,267 --> 00:49:05,733
-说真的，我好像
都能听见那车声了。
-我也是。
-I honestly believe
I can hear the car.
-I know.

852
00:49:05,767 --> 00:49:07,300
你能听到那台V12……
（模仿引擎轰鸣）
You can hear that V12...
(MIMICS ENGINE)

853
00:49:11,867 --> 00:49:14,033
终于，我们下了火车。
Finally, we were
off the train.

854
00:49:14,067 --> 00:49:17,900
现在是最后一程了，
坐大巴！
Now, for the last leg,
in a bus!

855
00:49:17,933 --> 00:49:19,867
噢，在隧道里听着真爽。
Ooh, it sounds good
in a tunnel.

856
00:49:20,867 --> 00:49:23,667
我这是在干嘛？
这可是在瑞士的隧道里啊！
What am I doing?
I'm in a Swiss tunnel!

857
00:49:23,700 --> 00:49:28,167
在这里的隧道里挂三挡狂飙，
我怕是得坐上
三十年牢。
I could go to prison
for 30 years for being in
third gear in a tunnel here.

858
00:49:28,200 --> 00:49:29,633
-咱们要去哪儿来着？
-韦尔比耶。
-Where is it we're going?
-Verbier.

859
00:49:29,667 --> 00:49:32,933
只落后他们40英里了！
Only 40 miles behind them!

860
00:49:34,600 --> 00:49:35,967
哈蒙德：
我有主意了。我搞定了。
HAMMOND:
I've got it. I've done it.

861
00:49:37,267 --> 00:49:40,167
天哪，太刺激了。
真刺激。
God, this is exciting.
This is exciting.

862
00:49:40,200 --> 00:49:42,867
眼前是阿尔卑斯山，
日内瓦已被我甩在身后。
I've got the Alps,
I've got Geneva behind me.

863
00:49:42,900 --> 00:49:46,700
穿越险峻的隧道，
还有大圣伯纳德山口。
I've got bold tunnels,
Grand Saint Bernard Pass.

864
00:49:47,867 --> 00:49:49,400
简直就像间谍惊悚大片一样。
It's all like a spy thriller.

865
00:49:49,433 --> 00:49:52,933
而我正在赛跑，
开着一辆法拉利！
And I'm in a race,
in a Ferrari!

866
00:49:52,967 --> 00:49:57,467
好了，我现在过了蒙特勒，
正沿着日内瓦湖岸飞驰。
Okay, I'm now past Montreux,
on the Lake Geneva shoreline.

867
00:49:57,500 --> 00:50:00,867
# 瑞士时间所剩无几 #
# Swiss time is running out

868
00:50:00,900 --> 00:50:04,733
# 我们心知大势已去 #
# We knew that we would
lose the race #

869
00:50:04,767 --> 00:50:10,300
其实差得远呢，因为
他们得坐着大巴慢吞吞爬上
12英里的盘山公路。
Far from it, actually, because
they had to get up 12 miles
of mountain road in a bus.

870
00:50:10,333 --> 00:50:13,333
而我正开着一辆法拉利
疯狂追捕他们。
And I was hunting them down
in a Ferrari.

871
00:50:15,867 --> 00:50:17,867
切到手动，
开启运动模式。
Switching to manual,
and sport.

872
00:50:17,900 --> 00:50:23,133
我们得榨干这台车能提供的
所有潜能，
而它的底子深不可测。
We're gonna need everything
this car has got to give,
and it's got a lot to give.

873
00:50:23,167 --> 00:50:24,967
他在后面。
我敢肯定他就在咱们后面！
He's behind.
I know he's behind us!

874
00:50:27,500 --> 00:50:29,033
十分钟车程，
外加走一小段路。
Ten minutes
plus a little walk.

875
00:50:30,367 --> 00:50:33,733
-我随时都在等那台V12的咆哮声。
-我也一样。
-I'm waiting to hear
the V12 wailing.
-I am, as well.

876
00:50:35,567 --> 00:50:39,933
-一旦看到法拉利的车灯，咱们就全完了！
-得了吧，别乌鸦嘴。
-We'll see a set of Ferrari
headlamps, and it's all over!
-Oh, c'mon.

877
00:50:41,867 --> 00:50:45,100
为了赢詹姆斯和理查德
搭上性命，值吗？
Is it worth dying to beat
James and Richard?

878
00:50:45,133 --> 00:50:47,133
不值。
No.

879
00:50:47,167 --> 00:50:50,867
但为了证明火车就是一堆废铁
搭上性命呢？太值了。
Is it worth dying to prove
trains are useless? Yes.

880
00:50:52,433 --> 00:50:54,467
-我要去替司机开大巴。
-别犯傻！
-I'm going to go
and drive the bus.
-No!

881
00:50:54,500 --> 00:50:56,467
克拉克森：这感觉太折磨人了。
CLARKSON: This was awful.

882
00:50:56,500 --> 00:51:00,367
我知道在这片夜色中的某个地方，
他们就领先我几分钟而已。
I knew that
somewhere in the darkness,
they were just minutes ahead.

883
00:51:00,400 --> 00:51:03,567
你看，我不知道韦尔比耶到底还有多远，
这才是最大的麻烦。
